# ==============================================================================
# REST Client Test File for Ticket Management API
# Extension: "REST Client" by Huachao Mao (humao.rest-client)
# Usage:
#   1. Click "Send Request" directly above any endpoint below.
#   2. The request response will appear in a side-by-side panel.
#   3. You can execute "Create a New Ticket" first, and subsequent requests
#      will automatically reuse the captured @ticketId!
# ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

###

### 2. List All Tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets

###

### 3. List Tickets Filtered by Status (OPEN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets?status=OPEN

###

### 4. List Tickets Filtered by Priority (HIGH)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets?priority=HIGH

###

### 5. Create a New Ticket (Captures ID for subsequent requests)
# @name createTicket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Setup OAuth2 Login with PKCE",
  "description": "Allow users to authenticate using Google or GitHub securely",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "assignee": "Subit"
}

###

# Dynamically extract ticket ID from the createTicket response above!
@ticketId = {{createTicket.response.body.data.id}}

### 6. Get Created Ticket by Captured ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}

###

### 7. Update Ticket Details
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Setup OAuth2 Login with PKCE & Refresh Tokens",
  "priority": "CRITICAL"
}

###

### 8. Update Ticket Status (OPEN -> IN_PROGRESS)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

###

### 9. Update Ticket Status (IN_PROGRESS -> RESOLVED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}

###

### 10. Attempt Illegal Transition (RESOLVED -> OPEN is forbidden by state machine)
# Expected: HTTP 409 Conflict with error message
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/status
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "status": "OPEN"
}

###

### 11. Validation Error Demo (Title < 3 chars fails validation)
# Expected: HTTP 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "ab",
  "priority": "HIGH"
}

###

### 12. Delete the Created Ticket
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}

###

### 13. Verify Ticket is Deleted (Expected: HTTP 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}

###

### 14. Get Ticket Metrics & Statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tickets/metrics
